ility of the data for further use. ICP-MS is generally more sensitive for elements that are present at low concentrations than ICP-OES, and the former instrument was used to quantify As, Se, Mo and Cd.","label":"AfSIS I ICP Aqua regia Detection Limits.tab","restricted":false,"version":4,"datasetVersionId":1990,"dataFile":{"id":12234,"persistentId":"doi:10.34725/DVN/66BFOB/EYVSPP","pidURL":"https://doi.org/10.34725/DVN/66BFOB/EYVSPP","filename":"AfSIS I ICP Aqua regia Detection Limits.tab","contentType":"text/tab-separated-values","filesize":2062,"description":"Aqua regia (Quasi-total) extractions of soils:\r\n\r\nThese soil digests were analysed by both ICP-OES and by ICP-MS. Limit of Detection is 3x standard deviation of blank samples expressed as mg/kg, assuming 0.25 g sample to volume 25 ml. The Quantitation Limit is 10x standard deviation of blank samples expressed as mg/kg.\r\n\r\nUsers who download the data can consider these limits to decide on the reliability of the data for further use. ICP-MS is generally more sensitive for elements that are present at low concentrations than ICP-OES, and the former instrument was used to quantify As, Se, Mo and Cd.","storageIdentifier":"file://19976f247e4-871c88a2ed69","originalFileFormat":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","originalFormatLabel":"MS Excel Spreadsheet","originalFileSize":10445,"UNF":"UNF:6:er9xltBjodTkRnTr8kOj6w==","rootDataFileId":-1,"md5":"df7a01bf4200a408c03280800f7d40bb","checksum":{"type":"MD5","value":"df7a01bf4200a408c03280800f7d40bb"},"creationDate":"2025-09-23"}},{"label":"Variables_Description.tab","restricted":false,"version":4,"datasetVersionId":1990,"dataFile":{"id":11219,"persistentId":"doi:10.34725/DVN/66BFOB/E1OELB","pidURL":"https://doi.org/10.34725/DVN/66BFOB/E1OELB","filename":"Variables_Description.tab","contentType":"text/tab-separated-values","filesize":6275,"storageIdentifier":"file://177616628f5-e2140cc649fe","originalFileFormat":"application/vnd.ope